\begin{description}
\item[* name:] Tauxtocomp2
\item[* relevant examples:] (YOU) Don't open the door $\rightarrow$ Don't
(YOU) open the door
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) 
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] 
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class)
\item[* date of creation:] 13-JUN-1991 16:44:26  
\item[* author:] Petra de Wit
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To move negated do (either incorporated or not) into conjrel. 
Notice that positive 'do' 
should not be raised, since then it would not be deleted in Tdodeletion, 
yielding the not ungrammatical, but improper translation "DO open the door".
This type of imperative should get a special translation into Dutch and has not 
been dealt with yet.
