\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TCanNegIncorp
< m1: SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ mu1,
                I1:auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu2],
                negrel/NEG(KEY_notNEGkey){NEGrec1},
                mu3
              ]
>

< m : SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ mu1,
                auxrel/VERB{VERBrec2}
                      [ I1:head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu2],
                        gluerel/GLUE{GLUErec1},
                        negrel/NEG(KEY_not2NEGkey){NEGrec2}
                      ],
                mu3
              ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: VERBrec1.subc IN [modalverb] AND 
           EXIST (mu2, [head/SUBVERB{SUBVERBrec1}
                            [I11:head/BVERB(KEY1){BVERBrec1}] ])
         I11: KEY1 = KEY_can1BVERBkey OR
              KEY1 = KEY_can2BVERBkey
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec1.tense = presenttense
          A1: VERBrec2 := VERBrec1;
              VERBrec2.subc := notaux
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: VERBrec1.tense = presenttense AND
              VERBrec2 = VERBrec1 EXCEPT FOR [subc] AND
              VERBrec2.subc = notaux
          A1: @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TCanNegIncorp
\item[* relevant examples:] 
He can not sing $\rightarrow$ he cannot sing 
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] ClauseToSentence
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_NegAuxAdapt
\item[* date of creation:] 9-FEB-1989 14:00:20  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] TNegAuxAdapt
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to contract the negation to the modal {\em can\/} to form {\em 
cannot\/}, in case no 
inversion took place ($^{*}$Cannot you come?), so this transformation is ordered 
crucially after TC\_AuxToComp. The form {\em can't\/} has been made before the 
inversion rules, since it can undergo inversion: {\em Can't you stop that\/}.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) It has not been 
decided yet whether the transformation should be optional (as it is now), 
or should work in 
analysis only. A filter FPreCanNegIncorp has been written to ensure that no
incorporated {\em nòt} remains in analysis.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
