\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] FPreCanNegIncorp
\item[* relevant examples:] He cannot do that
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] ClauseToSentence
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_NegAuxAdapt
\item[* date of creation:] 25-OCT-1989 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] 
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to stop any sentence (in analysis) that has {\em cannot\/}, 
since this string must be reanalysed as {\em can\/} + a different {\em not\/}
(to be able to distinguish between {\em can't\/} and {\em cannot\/}).
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
